      },
      "id": 18,
      "options": {
        "content": "**N/A on any panel means unknown or not evaluated — never zero.** No panel uses a zero fallback, and no profit series is fabricated when components are missing. Every panel is an instantaneous gauge snapshot of the latest valid report (the history panel simply repeats those snapshots over time): these are not return series, and nothing here is annualized.\n\n- **Fees** are a declared scenario (study config: 5 bps/side, 0 USD/contract), charged once per fill — not a venue schedule; regulatory components and eligibility are unverified.\n- **Funding** is a declared hourly-rate sensitivity over signed perpetual notional × contract time. Public funding observations do not establish published-vs-projected, payment reference or actual postings — this is not cashflow, and scenarios are never summed.\n- **Settlement** is never inferred: dated positions never settle in this pipeline; expiry with open exposure stays `expired_with_open_exposure` and contributes no settlement PnL.\n- **Marks** are last observed single-site L2 mids — scenario marks, not executable exits; a missing mark withholds unrealized and net excess instead of writing zero.\n- **Capital** is account-level committed paper cash including the idle buffer, not a margin requirement; span/hurdle/interest are withheld across clock ambiguity.\n- **Outside these numbers:** unmodeled infrastructure/cloud and account-specific costs are subtracted nowhere here.\n- **No annualized return** is claimed anywhere; net excess is a scenario decomposition for one explicit intent set and one selected funding rate, before the costs above.\n\nProgress and quality evidence: [progress and data quality](/d/market-research-progress) · Operational capture: [capture health](/d/market-recorder-capture) · Method: [review plan §6](https://github.com/paulkiernan/diff-logic-cells/blob/main/research/MEASUREMENT_REVIEW_PLAN.md)",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Unknowns, limits and exclusions",
      "type": "text"
    }
